    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and expand it to the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials).\n\nFirst, distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term individually:\n\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot 7 = 21x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = -6x^3\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot 7 = -35x\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x \\cdot (-2x) = 10x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 7 = 28\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot (-2x) = -8x\n\\]\n\nNext, we add all these terms together:\n\n\\[\n21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nNow, combine like terms:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nWe have the expression in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\). Therefore, we identify the coefficients:\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nAdd the numbers together:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 = 76\n\\]\n\\[\n76 - 86 = -10\n\\]\n\\[\n-10 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nFinally, the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
